From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:34:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: keep the first error in the shutdown
 dance and always undo it

tas2764_do_quirky_pwr_ctrl_change() chained its steps on !ret, and the
shutdown write in the middle is an update_bits() that returns 1 when it
changes the register. So on every real ACTIVE or MUTE -> SHUTDOWN
transition the post sequence was skipped: 0xfd:0x64 stayed at 4. The
final update_bits() then overwrote ret, so a failed pre sequence was
lost as well.

Treat only a negative value as an error, keep the first one, and always
run the post sequence once the pre sequence has been tried, so 0xfd:0x64
goes back to 0 and the hidden page is deselected even when a step before
it failed. Return 0 on success. The helper is reachable from the device
tree for the first time with apple,shutdown-dance.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit 66ffe5f045541c94024c8824256b4dd1793154a1)
(cherry picked from commit 5891a3f9c63656d21ab184c71117a778e14d9903)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764-quirks.h | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764-quirks.h b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764-quirks.h
index 7a62b3ba5b4..25d2e8d5313 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764-quirks.h
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764-quirks.h
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ static int tas2764_do_quirky_pwr_ctrl_change(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764,
 					     unsigned int target)
 {
 	unsigned int curr;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, err;
 
 	curr = snd_soc_component_read_field(tas2764->component,
 					       TAS2764_PWR_CTRL,
@@ -129,26 +129,37 @@ static int tas2764_do_quirky_pwr_ctrl_change(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764,
 	if (target == curr)
 		return 0;
 
-	/* Handle power state transition to shutdown */
+	/*
+	 * Handle power state transition to shutdown. update_bits() returns 1
+	 * when it changed the register, so only a negative value is an error.
+	 * Keep the first error, and always run the post sequence so that
+	 * 0xfd:0x64 is put back and the hidden page deselected, even when a
+	 * step before it failed.
+	 */
 	if (target == TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_SHUTDOWN &&
 	   (curr == TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MUTE || curr == TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_ACTIVE)) {
 		ret = regmap_multi_reg_write(tas2764->regmap, tas2764_pre_shutdown_seq,
 					ARRAY_SIZE(tas2764_pre_shutdown_seq));
+		if (!ret) {
+			err = snd_soc_component_update_bits(tas2764->component,
+							    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL,
+							    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MASK,
+							    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_SHUTDOWN);
+			if (err < 0)
+				ret = err;
+		}
+		err = regmap_multi_reg_write(tas2764->regmap,
+					     tas2764_post_shutdown_seq,
+					     ARRAY_SIZE(tas2764_post_shutdown_seq));
 		if (!ret)
-			ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(tas2764->component,
-							TAS2764_PWR_CTRL,
-							TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MASK,
-							TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_SHUTDOWN);
-		if (!ret)
-			ret = regmap_multi_reg_write(tas2764->regmap,
-						tas2764_post_shutdown_seq,
-						ARRAY_SIZE(tas2764_post_shutdown_seq));
+			ret = err;
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(tas2764->component, TAS2764_PWR_CTRL,
-						    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MASK, target);
+					    TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_MASK, target);
 
-	return ret;
+	return ret < 0 ? ret : 0;
 }
 
 /*
